<title>BRAZIL: SOCCER-LIBERTADORES CUP RESULTS/STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-LIBERTADORES CUP RESULTS/STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-03-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of South</p>
<p>American Libertadores Cup first round, group two matches</p>
<p>played Sunday:</p>
<p>In Quito: Nacional (Ecuador) 2 Racing Club (Argentina) 0</p>
<p>(halftime 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Simon Ruiz (35), Kleber Chala (62)</p>
<p>In Guayaquil, Ecuador: Emelec (Ecuador) 2 Velez Sarsfield</p>
<p>(Argentina) 3 (2-2)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Emelec - Ariel Graziani (9, penalty), Carlos Juarez (45)</p>
<p>Velez Sarsfield - Patrico Camps (3 and 66), Martin Posse</p>
<p>(21)</p>
<p>Standings (tabulate under played, won, drawn, lost, goals</p>
<p>for, goals against, points)</p>
<p> Nacional		3  2  1  0  5  2  7</p>
<p> Velez Sarsfield     3  2  0  1  5  4  6</p>
<p> Emelec		  3  0  2  1  6  7  2</p>
<p> Racing Club	   3  0  1  2  3  6  1</p>
<p>Note: top three teams qualify for the second round.</p>
</text>
